# Runtime command safety (containers)

## Rule (guardrail)

This plugin targets **containerized Node/TS/JS** repos. Many runtime commands are environment-specific.

- Do NOT run Node/npm commands automatically on the **host** (e.g. `node`, `npm`, `npx`) when the project uses container-only npm — see `00-shared-node-npm-container-only.mdc`.
- Do NOT run Docker / compose commands automatically without confirming the service/workdir (e.g. `docker`, `docker compose`).
- Do NOT invent PHP/Composer/PHPUnit command recipes — this plugin is Node/TS/JS only.

Instead:
- Ask which container/service to use and the working directory (or read `DEVELOPMENT-LOCAL.md`).
- Prefer stable, repeatable command shapes from `runtime-commands-containers` / `node-npm-container-only`.

## Runbook

See `runtime-commands-containers` skill.
